hi I'm Evan Carmichael and welcome to  another edition of modeling the masters  today we're going to look at how a young  boy from a family of ten in Mississippi  was always looking out for opportunities  and turned a fifteen thousand dollar  investment into a multi-billion dollar  empire  this is a story of Robert Johnson and a  top three lessons that you can learn  from his success Robert Johnson is an  American businessman best known for  being the founder of television network  block entertainment television  eet in 2001 Johnson became the first  African American billionaire and the  first black person to be listed on any  of Forbes as a world's rich list Johnson  was born in Mississippi and was a ninth  of 10 children according to Johnson we  weren't a well firm family but we knew  that if we wanted a bicycle and when  somebody else wasn't going to get  something else if you wanted to go to  college  you knew your parents couldn't pay your  way he had an entrepreneurial Drive and  used his $15,000 in savings to launch B  et in 1980 it started with only two  hours of old movies each Friday in fact  for the first five years speed he would  lose money soon however it began to  expand his programming and cable  operators jumped on board they believed  that many of their subscribers would be  interested in watching block oriented  shows eleven years after its initial  launch B et became the first black owned  company to be listed on a New York Stock  Exchange today B et has spin-off  channels and is the largest black-owned  cable company in history  Johnson bought back all the BT stock  seven years after went public for 1  billion dollars he then sold it to media  giant Viacom two years later for three  billion dollars  by always looking for opportunities and  by starting small Johnson turned a  fifteen thousand dollar investment into  a fortune to help you build on your  opportunities here are three action  items you can learn from Robert Johnson  action item number one always be growing  as entrepreneurs we need to always be  finding new customers and growing our  businesses whether it's launching new  products offering more services  aggressively marketing your existing  solutions need to always be growing  Johnson has been called a serial  entrepreneur thanks to his love of  starting new businesses on-the-fly  throughout his career however if there  has been one thing that he's learned  it's this there are always new customers  to go after according to Johnson if  there's something I can do and I feel it  should be done I just want to do it I  just don't want to leave it undone  because I'll sit back and say why didn't  I do that why didn't I start that  business action item number two be  opportunistic entrepreneurs are the  special individuals who can spot  opportunities and then turn them into  profitable businesses in order to start  a new company or grow your existing one  you should always have an eye out for  new opportunities where Johnson sees a  chance to make money he jumps at it no  if ands or buts about it  while his critics use that fact as one  more chance to knock him down  Johnson attributes his success largely  to his opportunism Johnson is an  entrepreneur plain and simple he wants  to make money and lots of it  according to Johnson whenever I see an  opportunity and a chance to change  something I go at it be et was never a  legacy event for me  BT was something I started as an  investment and I knew someday I would  sell it  action um number three ignore your  critics if you're doing something  different then you're gonna have your  critics people are going to attack you  for your ideas and try to knock you down  it's gonna come from our competitors and  in many cases even come from our friends  and family Johnson had a lot of critics  as he built his business one of his  greatest successes in his own mind he's  been in Africa merican who succeeded at  the highest level since he felt that  nobody expects minorities to be there as  much as others tried to paint his career  in terms of black and white johnson has  refused to let others identify him as  anything other than an entrepreneur and  a good one at that according to Johnson  today if I were to put on jeans and walk  into a jewelry store and I could  probably buy the jewelry store ten times  over but the jeweler is gonna look at me  as a black guy in jeans who probably  can't afford it and maybe who just might  steal something so remember always be  growing be opportunistic and ignore your  critics to finish up this video I wanted  to share one of my favorite true stories  about Robert Johnson and some of his  best quotes after being the first in his  family to go to college  Johnson plan to start a career as a  government worker that all changed from  the national cable and  Telecommunications Association hired  Johnson as a lobbyist for the nascent  cable industry that experience proved to  be a wake-up call for Johnson he began  to think about his own opportunity to  create a cable channel just for  african-americans and would soon go on  to launch be ETA  thank you for joining me for another  edition of modeling the masters if you  enjoyed the video please give it a  thumbs up I'd also love to hear thoughts  and feedback if you want to leave a  comment below the video and stay tuned  to the next episode  you
 

